> 8 and neither appears in the product grid. Searching \\\"macrame\\\" (sold prod-5's title) returns \\\"0 items available / No items found\\\", so sold and deleted listings are unreachable to buyers via browse or search and cannot be added to a cart or used to start a request.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-5\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Registered Tim Tester / tim.tester@example.com / secret123 / Brooklyn, NY. Toast \\\"Account created successfully!\\\", redirected to home, header switched to authenticated state (Sell + cart + user menu).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-6\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No maximum-price filter; the price control is a single-thumb slider that only sets a minimum\", \"actual\": \"The \\\"Price Range\\\" control renders one thumb only (aria-valuenow=0, min=0, max=500) and its label is always \\\"$X - $500\\\": moving it changed the label $0->$10->$130 and filtered to items priced >= $130 (prod-10 $320, prod-3 $175, prod-4 $180). The $500 upper bound cannot be lowered, so a buyer cannot set a maximum price. All other criteria worked correctly: Furniture -> 2 furniture items; upcycled + Like New -> only prod-8; distance <=10mi -> exactly the 6 items with distance 4-9, excluding prod-2 (15mi) and prod-6 (12mi); sorts newest/price-low ($35..$320)/price-high ($320..$35)/distance (4,5,6,7,8,9) all ordered correctly.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"\\\"AUSTIN\\\" (uppercase) -> 3 results, all Austin, TX (location match). \\\"LeVi's\\\" (mixed case) -> only prod-2, matched via description \\\"Classic 90s Levi's denim jacket\\\" (title/description match). Clearing the query restored the full 8 available items.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"As Emma added Marcus's prod-2 ($65) and prod-9 ($35) — neither owned by her. Clicking Add to Cart twice on prod-2 kept the badge at 1 (no duplicate line). Cart shows \\\"2 items\\\", line rows render photo + title + \\\"San Francisco, CA\\\" + $65, and total $100.00 = 65+35.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"As Emma on Marcus's prod-2 (available, not owned): \\\"Message Seller\\\" opened dialog \\\"Send a message to Marcus Chen\\\"; Send Message was disabled while the textarea was empty (non-empty enforced), enabled after typing; sending closed the dialog and showed the toast \\\"Message sent to seller!\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-21\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Category cards on the /categories page do not apply the chosen category to browse results\", \"actual\": \"The /categories page correctly advertises \\\"Furniture 2 items\\\", but clicking it navigates to /?category=furniture and the browse section still lists all 8 available items across every category (sports, clothing, home-decor, electronics, toys, books) with the count reading \\\"8 items available\\\" and the Furniture filter checkbox still unchecked. The ?category= query parameter is ignored. By contrast the home page's own Furniture tile correctly filters to \\\"2 items available\\\", so the defect is specific to the category-browsing page.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-22\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"No seller-facing view of purchase requests, and cart requests are reported as sent without any request being recorded\", \"actual\": \"(a) Emma sent a request on Marcus's prod-2 (stored in app state as req-1787907223118 with the buyer message). Signing in as Marcus, no surface shows it: My Listings lists only his items, the owner product page shows only listing data, and the \\\"My Profile\\\" menu item leads to a 404 \\\"Oops! Page not found\\\". The message text never appears (body.innerText.includes('QA-MARKER-77') === false on every seller screen). (b) As Marcus, adding prod-1 and prod-5 to the cart and clicking \\\"Send Purchase Request\\\" emptied the cart and toasted \\\"Purchase requests sent to sellers!\\\", yet the in-memory requests array still held only the single pre-existing prod-2 request — zero requests were created for the two cart items.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-10\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Login with nobody.unregistered@example.com rejected: \\\"Invalid credentials. Try: emma@example.com\\\"; stayed on /login, header still shows Log in/Sign up (no session).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-11\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Registering \\\"EMMA@Example.com\\\" (case variation of existing emma@example.com) rejected with \\\"An account with this email already exists\\\"; stayed on /register, no session created, existing account untouched.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Password is never verified; any password authenticates a registered account\", \"actual\": \"Signed in as emma@example.com with the deliberately wrong password \\\"totally-wrong-password-xyz\\\". App redirected to / and the header changed to the authenticated state (Sell link, no Log in/Sign up), proving an authenticated session was created despite an incorrect password.\", \"evidence\": \"Login page openly advertises \\\"(any password works)\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"As Emma viewing Marcus's prod-2: only Add to Cart + Message Seller exposed, no edit/delete/mark-sold controls. On her own prod-1 the buyer actions are replaced by a \\\"Manage Your Listings\\\" link. Owner-only management confirmed.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-14\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Empty submit blocked by native required validation on title/description/price (:invalid). Missing category/condition blocked with toast \\\"Please fill in all required fields\\\". Missing photo blocked with specific toast \\\"Please add at least one image\\\". No listing created in any case.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Price input is type=number min=0 step=0.01. Price \\\"-50\\\" blocked with validationMessage \\\"Value must be greater than or equal to 0.\\\"; no listing created. Non-numeric \\\"abc\\\" is not accepted by the field (coerced to empty) and then blocked as a missing required field.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-23\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Guarded pages render a blank white screen instead of a sign-in prompt or redirect\", \"actual\": \"Two of the four guarded surfaces work: Add to Cart while signed out redirects to /login, and the Message Seller send button is disabled and labelled \\\"Log in to message\\\". But visiting /cart or /create-listing while signed out leaves the URL unchanged and renders a completely empty document (document.body.innerText.trim().length === 0) — no sign-in prompt, no redirect, no content. Console shows React Router's \\\"You should call navigate() in a React.useEffect(), not when your component is first rendered\\\", indicating a broken redirect guard.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-16\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Duplicate-email error appeared immediately above the form without navigation; all four fields remained populated and editable for correction.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Typing into the search box updated the grid and the \\\"N items available\\\" counter live (10->0 for \\\"macrame\\\", 3 for \\\"AUSTIN\\\", 1 for \\\"LeVi's\\\", back to 8 when cleared) with no Enter press or submit button.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Every filter/sort change re-rendered the grid and the \\\"N items available\\\" counter instantly with no submit or reload (category 8->2, upcycled+condition ->1, price min ->3, distance ->6, sort reorders). \\\"Clear all filters\\\" reset price to \\\"$0 - $500\\\", distance to \\\"Any\\\" and restored all 8 available listings.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-19\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Add to Cart showed toast \\\"Added to cart!\\\" instantly and the header badge went from empty to 1, then 2, with no reload. Cart page then reflected both line items, count \\\"2 items\\\" and total $100.00.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CT-20\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"prod-1 detail renders all required fields consistently with its data: multiple photos (gallery + thumbnails with prev/next), title \\\"Mid-Century Modern Armchair\\\", full description, $285, category Furniture (also in breadcrumb), condition \\\"Like New\\\", location \\\"Brooklyn, NY (2.5 mi)\\\", seller \\\"Emma Green\\\" with seller location, \\\"Listed 2024-11-20\\\", and an \\\"Upcycled\\\" badge (isUpcycled=true). Availability is reflected too: after marking it sold the page shows \\\"This item is no longer available\\\", while available listings instead expose Add to Cart. Non-upcycled prod-2 correctly shows no Upcycled badge.\"}]}"
